  "tape": "after_dark_1",
  "notes": "Ro's night show opener: the brightest and bounciest tape. It opens On Air with Bell's station jingle on vibraphone over a held D6/9, and the A theme is that jingle re-sung over the changes. Finger snaps on 2 and 4, the swingiest hats and shaker of the catalogue, off-beat Rhodes stabs and a bouncing bass; faster chord changes (two per bar at phrase ends), cassette hiss instead of vinyl, and a presence lift that gives it the brightest top end of any track.",
